;; rsi's lowering level's classes (bin/rsi lower-check; doc/rust/EVAL.md §7, RE2): every UI program whose lowered build does not
;; run as the original falls into one, the first whose :match finds its "RESULT REASON" (arbace.rust.check's judge; goi's format,
;; RES13 (a)). :kind :design (by design) or :deferred (a later milestone or proposal names it). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :native-unwind
  :title "a panic through lowered frames with the native std"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "RE2 links the lowered program with the host's native std (EVAL.md §4): its panics unwind natively through the lowered frames, which have unwind tables but no personality, so their landing pads (drops while unwinding, Drop impls that print, a panic in a drop) do not run, and a catch inlined into lowered code (no __rust_try left: -O builds) catches nothing (std aborts: failed to initiate panic); RE3's pending-flag layer runs them"
  :decided "RES4 (a); RE3"
  :match [#"^differs .*\(the original panics\)" #"^differs .*\(no native frame catches the panic\)"
          #"^differs .*\(the lowered build panics; a Drop in the test\)"]}
 {:id :known-bug
  :title "tests of rustc's known bugs"
  :kind :design
  :why "compiletest's known-bug tests record a miscompilation (LLVM's optimizations of the IR, as `-Copt-level=2` builds it); the lowered build, gcc -O0 of what the IR says, does not reproduce it"
  :decided "RES2 (c)"
  :match [#"^differs .*\(a known-bug test\)"]}
 {:id :inline-asm
  :title "inline assembly"
  :kind :design
  :why "asm! and global_asm! are the target's machine code: the lowering takes only the empty barrier (asm sideeffect \"\"); asm goto (callbr) and every other template are refused, as for C++ (LLVM 23's module asm(target_cpu: ...) header, global_asm!'s, is not read by repr/llvm)"
  :decided "survey §5.3, §8.2"
  :match [#"^refused refused inline-asm " #"^refused refused instruction llvm: .*the instruction callbr"
          #"^refused refused parse llvm: .*\(at \"target_cpu\"\)"]}
 {:id :simd
  :title "vector shapes the lowering refuses"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "fixed-width vectors are lowered element by element (RES6 (a)); masked loads and stores, gathers, scatters and core::arch's llvm.x86 intrinsics are not yet"
  :decided "RES6 (a); RE5"
  :match [#"^refused refused (vector|intrinsic lower: llvm\.(masked|x86)\.)"]}
 {:id :float16-128
  :title "f16 and f128"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the nightly types f16 and f128 (LLVM half and fp128): C forms' _Float16 and _Float128 are not in the lowering's arithmetic yet"
  :decided "survey §8.2"
  :match [#"^refused refused float-type .*(half|fp128)" #"^refused refused type .*(half|fp128)"]}
 {:id :c-variadic
  :title "C-variadic Rust functions"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a Rust function with C's `...` (c_variadic) defines its own va_list; the lowering takes va_start only after a named parameter"
  :decided "RE5"
  :match [#"^refused refused va "]}
 {:id :alias
  :title "aliases of variables"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "an LLVM alias of a variable or an expression (externally implementable items' statics): the lowering takes function aliases only, as for C++"
  :decided "RE5"
  :match [#"^refused refused alias "]}
 {:id :lto
  :title "link-time optimization"
  :kind :design
  :why "-C lto splits the program into codegen units the link merges; rsi lowers one unit's IR (-C codegen-units=1 does not hold under thin LTO)"
  :decided "EVAL.md §1"
  :match [#"^refused refused cgu "]}
 {:id :wide-int
  :title "integers wider than 128 bits"
  :kind :design
  :why "LLVM's optimizations (a test's -C opt-level with fat LTO) make integers of 256 bits and more out of memory copies; C forms' widest is __int128: the lowering refuses them, as for C++; rsi's own builds are -O0"
  :decided "RES2 (a)"
  :match [#"^refused refused wide-int "]}
 {:id :optimized-ir
  :title "shapes of optimized IR"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a test's own -C opt-level with fat LTO puts std's optimized code in the program's IR: vector getelementptrs and static initializers whose constant expressions gcc does not fold; rsi's IR is -O0's (RES2 (a)), these shapes are the lowering's later tail"
  :decided "RES2 (c); RE5"
  :match [#"^refused refused gep .*\(vector " #"^gcc gcc .*initializer element is not constant"]}
 {:id :speed
  :title "beyond the build's time"
  :kind :design
  :why "programs whose IR the lowering, evaluated on stage 0, does not finish within the build's 300 s (a 32 MiB constant)"
  :decided "survey §8.2"
  :match [#"^build build the lowering did not finish"]}
]
